# Python's bytecode cache, written beside a tools/*.py module that another
# script imports: a by-product of running the tools, never source.
__pycache__/

# Running the application against a sample writes a backup beside its project.
# The samples are inputs, not working directories.
samples/*/backups/

# Third-party reference material under its author's own licence, kept on disk
# and never in the repository: the reference customisation in the legacy
# formats (two style libraries and two survey code files, with their colour
# table), which resources/customisation/ below is made from. The build reads
# nothing here. One suite does, through KATANA_REFERENCE_CUSTOMISATION_DIR:
# the converter's test of what it makes of these files
# (tests/archive12d/customisation/test_convert.cpp), which skips where the
# folder is absent or holds no such file.
docs/12d Refrence Files/

# The TfNSW Utility Schema and Specification workbook (DMS-FT-493), under
# TfNSW's licence: kept on disk, never in the repository. The cli.utility_check
# tests read it when it is there (src/katana_app/CMakeLists.txt) and are not
# registered when it is not; tools/utility_schema_domains.py reads any copy.
docs/TfNSW Reference Files/

# The customisation compiled into the build: nsw.customisation.json, the one
# file in the Katana customisation format that katana_customisation_convert
# makes of the reference files above (docs/customisation.md, "The reference
# customisation"), compiled in with #embed through
# KATANA_BUILTIN_CUSTOMISATION. It is made from third-party material under its
# own licence, so it is kept on disk and never in the repository; a checkout
# without it builds a program with no built-in customisation.
#
# The older embedding still looks in this folder as well
# (tools/embed_customisation.py, through KATANA_CUSTOMISATION_DIR), for the
# four legacy files it was written for: linestyles.4d, symbols.4d,
# survey_codes.mapfile and survey_codes_names.mapfile. They are no longer kept
# here, so it builds an empty table and the tests that read it skip. They are
# not to be copied back in beside the converted file: the tests that hand
# every file of this folder to the legacy loader would then fail on it
# (docs/building.md, "The reference folder and the converter").
resources/customisation/

# Git worktrees created for parallel agents (CLAUDE.md section 8). Each is a
# checkout of its own; tracking one would embed a repository in this one.
.claude/worktrees/

# GDAL's persistent auxiliary metadata: statistics it caches beside a raster
# it has read. A by-product, and a stale one - samples/gis/terrain.asc.aux.xml
# was committed by accident and held approximate statistics the DEM does not
# have (audit IO-13). Katana no longer asks GDAL to write them.
samples/**/*.aux.xml
